---
import createBackup from "../../captures/create-backup.png";
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
---

<GuidePage slug="backups-and-storage" lead="Katari keeps downloads, automatic backups and your own comics in one folder you choose.">
  <Task id="storage-folder" title="The storage folder">
    <p>
      Setup asks for it, and <Path>Settings › Data and storage › Storage location</Path> changes it. Give Katari a folder of its own; it
      fills it like this:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`Katari/
  autobackup/                 automatic backups
  downloads/
    Pepper&Carrot (EN)/       comics, one folder per source
    Blender Studio [anime]/   video
    Gutenberg [book]/         books
  local/                      your own comics`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Inside, each title has a folder of its own. After moving or deleting files there yourself, tap <Path>Settings › Advanced › Reindex
      downloads</Path> so Katari notices.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="backup" title="Back up" shot={{ image: createBackup, alt: "What a backup can keep, each with a box to tick", caption: "Create backup" }}>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <Path>Settings › Data and storage</Path> and tap <strong>Create backup</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tick what to keep: library entries, chapters, tracking, history, categories, app settings, extension stores and source settings.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Include sensitive settings (e.g., tracker login tokens)</strong> adds logins and other private settings. Keep a backup with
        them somewhere only you can reach.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>A backup always holds every profile.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="automatic" title="Automatic backups">
    <p>
      Katari backs up by itself every 12 hours and keeps the last four in <code>autobackup/</code>, named like
      <code>katari_2026-10-13_09-30.tachibk</code>. Change how often under <strong>Automatic backup frequency</strong>.
    </p>
    <Callout label="No logins">
      <p>Automatic backups never include sensitive settings. After restoring one, log in to your trackers again.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="left-out" title="What a backup leaves out">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Left out</th> <th>After a restore</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Downloads</strong></td> <td>Keep the storage folder, or download again</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Extensions and their trust</strong></td> <td>Install them again and trust each one</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Translation servers and API keys</strong></td> <td>Enter them again</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Text recognition models</strong></td> <td>They download again when a page needs them</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Sensitive settings</strong>, unless ticked</td> <td>Log in to trackers and sources again</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Task>

  <Task id="restore" title="Restore">
    <ol>
      <li>Tap <strong>Restore backup</strong> in <Path>Settings › Data and storage</Path>, or in setup, and pick the <code>.tachibk</code> file.</li>
      <li>Choose what to bring back: library, categories, app settings, extension stores, source settings.</li>
      <li>Katari then lists missing sources and trackers you aren't logged into. Install those extensions and log in.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Backups from Mihon and Tachiyomi restore the same way. Old JSON backups don't.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="mihon" title="Move from Mihon">
    <p>If Mihon is on the phone when you first open Katari, setup offers <strong>Move from Mihon</strong>:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap <strong>Open Mihon to create a backup</strong> and create one with everything you want to keep. Include private settings to bring source preferences and sign-ins.</li>
      <li>Back in Katari, tap <strong>Choose Mihon backup</strong> and pick it.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Extensions shared with Mihon stay available; ones installed privately in Mihon need installing again in Katari.</p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
